Pakman performs large-scale genomic assembly through k-mer counting and contig generation. The original MPI code
can be found at https://github.com/pnnl/pakman, as well as a references to technical publications describing the
algorithm and data structures used.

The SHAD implementation uses SHAD multimaps to store macro nodes, modified nodes, and wire nodes where the maps'
keys are kmer strings.  The list of macro nodes processed by an iteration is stored in the ProcessedNodes set.

Key Files -

1) include/graph.h - defines the BasePairVector, MultiNode, ModifiedNode, and WireNode classes and their methods.
2) tools/workflow3.cc - the main program.
3) workflow3/readFasta.cc - a method to read fasta file and initialize the macro node multimap.
4) workflow3/macroNode.cc - methods to count number of kmers of different lengths, construct macro nodes, modify
   macro nodes, wire macro nodes, delete macro nodes.
5) workflow3/process.cc - method that examines each marco node and decides which ones are ready for processing.
   For selected node, the modifications imparteds on other nodes is computed and stored in the ModifiedNodes mul-
   timap and its key is inserted in the ProcessedNodes set in preparation for deletion.

Input file - ecoli/ecoli_illumina_10x_part_.fasta

Input parameters -

1) FASTA input file name
2) kmer length
3) coverage
4) minimum length count
5) node threshold 

Run script (I use on our home cluster) -

salloc --cpu-freq=Performance -N 8 -p all mpirun -np 16 -npernode 2 --bind-to socket --mca mpi_cuda_support 0 \
/bin/do-workflow3 --gmt_num_workers 8 --gmt_num_helpers 1 --gmt_comm_buffer_size 4194304 \
/lustre/scratch/feo/wk3/ecoli_10.fasta 32 100 21 100000
